# Commits listed here are skipped by `git blame`, so a line's blame points at
# the commit that wrote the code rather than at a sweep that only moved
# whitespace. One full SHA per line; `#` starts a comment.
#
# GitHub reads this file by name and applies it to the blame view with no
# configuration. Local git does not -- each clone has to be pointed at it once:
#
#   git config blame.ignoreRevsFile .git-blame-ignore-revs
#
# Only list commits that changed formatting and nothing else, and only once the
# commit is on `main`. This repository merges by rebase, so a pull request's
# commit gets a new SHA when it lands; git silently skips a SHA it cannot
# resolve, so a branch SHA recorded here reads as correct and does nothing.
